@@ -0,0 +1,112 @@
+# Experimental source and reproduction record
+
+## Provenance and scope
+
+This is an independently published development snapshot of the contributor's
+broader Madeira experiment, based on willfaust/Madeira commit
+`279fd0f83170425db002fe25d6bd62f6355f497d`. Upstream history, licences and
+submodule pins are retained. The source manifest identifies the imported files.
+No FEX or DXMT source changes are introduced by this snapshot.
+
+The Wine submodule stays pinned at
+`9129e9684daaeae70da9435e7c6060e59392634e`. Its local diagnostics are provided as
+`build/experimental/wine-vulkan-diagnostics.patch`, under Wine's
+LGPL-2.1-or-later terms. Apply with the checked-in helper before rebuilding Wine
+native/PE components. This avoids a submodule pointer to an unpublished commit.
+
+MoltenVK is built from upstream commit
+`db66022459ffb663aa2b50f6b018bc2e124f5edf` (v1.4.2) plus the ten patches under
+`build/vulkan-ios/patches/`. Its upstream Apache-2.0 notices remain applicable.
+The scripts pin and hash the source-built input. These patches are experimental
+compatibility/cache/diagnostic policies, not a conformance implementation.
+
+Unlike the reduced, default-off upstream PR400, this broader experiment links
+Vulkan unconditionally. It also removes the permissive failed fixed-address
+reservation relocation path more broadly than PR396. Existing Social Club/CEF
+fallback behaviour can regress; this snapshot is not recommended as a general
+replacement for upstream Madeira. No game AppID/address patch or authentication
+bypass is introduced by the imported changes.
+
+## What was observed
+
+Earlier broader packages reached Detroit: Become Human's shader compilation,
+menu and an in-game scene on an Apple M5 iPad. The contributor confirmed camera
+control. A later WineVulkan queue-submit assertion remained. This is a report of
+limited device observations, not a full-game playability, performance or stability
+claim. The exact earlier successful game package is not reproduced by this source
+snapshot: diagnostics and later integer-output experiments were added afterwards.
+
+Separately, the reduced PR400 + PR399 Debug package was tested on the same iPad:
+real GPU enumeration, 16x16 RGBA8 clear with all 1024 bytes verified, and two visible
+RGB presentation rounds / 360 presentation calls passed, with guest exit0. Its
+App UUID was `777A5264-29FB-361D-9ED2-18B6A1048E97`. This validates that reduced
+route, not every policy in this larger snapshot. Post-exit JIT detach diagnostics
+remain a separate issue. Private raw logs/game images are not included here.
+
+## Building
+
+First read [the upstream prerequisites](BUILDING.md) and
+[the detailed Vulkan recipes](../build/vulkan-ios/README.md).
+The repository alone is not a complete bootstrap. Configured Wine host headers,
+llvm-mingw/Bison3, native FEX/DXMT/FFmpeg/FreeType/pairing inputs and Microsoft
+runtime resources are still required. Optional Wine Mono is separate.
+
+```sh
+git clone --recurse-submodules https://github.com/Jelly-RayTian/Madeira-Experimental.git
+cd Madeira-Experimental
+bash build/experimental/apply-wine-overlay.sh
+# Assemble/build the documented upstream prerequisites first.
+bash build/vulkan-ios/fetch.sh
+bash build/vulkan-ios/build-moltenvk-source.sh
+bash build/vulkan-ios/build.sh
+# Prepend your installed Bison3 and llvm-mingw bin directories to PATH.
+JOBS=2 bash build/wine-pe/build-modules.sh vulkan-1 winevulkan
+bash build/win32u-unix/build.sh
+bash build/ntdll-unix/build.sh
+bash build/wineserver/build.sh
+bash build/stage-licenses.sh
+xcodebuild -project app/Madeira.xcodeproj -scheme Madeira -configuration Debug \
+  -destination 'generic/platform=iOS' -derivedDataPath build/experimental/DerivedData \
+  CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO CODE_SIGNING_REQUIRED=NO CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY= DEVELOPMENT_TEAM= build
+```
+
+The native archive scripts consume generated Wine prerequisites; an incremental
+Xcode build alone does not rebuild them. Build real Vulkan PE DLLs after any stub
+DLL generation, which otherwise replaces the loader. Tracked inherited binaries
+are upstream artifacts, not updated experimental outputs. Rebuild affected
+components rather than treating a fresh clone's DLL farm as this experiment.
+
+Use Debug, then sign with your own real certificate/profile and enable JIT on the
+device. No certificate, profile or pairing file is distributed. Unsigned IPA
+releases are not published in this initial source release. Clean-machine and
+full independent-snapshot app rebuilds remain unverified.
+
+## Runtime configs
+
+`examples/detroit-baseline.cfg` contains the low-log baseline used in the local
+investigation. The zero-unbound-input compatibility policy deliberately chooses
+zeros for otherwise undefined input; visual correctness is not guaranteed.
+`examples/detroit-integer-output-experimental.cfg` additionally enables the newer
+integer-output policy and pipeline diagnostics. That newer policy has native Mac
+readback coverage; it is not established as fixing the later Detroit failure.
+Keep backups of your own settings, saves and caches. Changes to compiler/cache
+policies can trigger recompilation; no reliable compilation-speed improvement is
+claimed. Do not delete caches merely to match an example.
+
+Run the ordinary Windows x64 fixtures first; the generic sources are under
+`tests/x64/`, build and acceptance commands under `build/vulkan-ios/README.md`.
+The tests use Vulkan through Wine and MoltenVK, not a direct Metal substitute.
+Do not upload game executables, shader dumps or Steam/account data with reports.
+
+## Licensing and attribution
+
+Madeira and these Madeira-side changes use GPL-3.0-or-later with the Madeira
+Converter Exception in LICENSE-EXCEPTION.md. Wine-derived changes remain under
+Wine's LGPL-2.1-or-later terms; MoltenVK-derived patches retain its Apache-2.0
+terms. Existing notices, COPYING/LICENSE, LICENSES and THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md
+are preserved. Apple converter and Microsoft runtime distribution have separate
+terms; this source publication adds no new copies of those binaries.
+Work was prepared with AI assistance; device observations were supplied by the
+contributor. Do not submit AI-generated changes to FEX upstream; its contribution
+policy is distinct. This repository does not claim ownership of upstream Madeira,
+Wine, FEX, MoltenVK, or Detroit assets, and is not an official Quantic Dream port.
